  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "With the last update, the precision of Object Sync's position on remote clients has become very low. Traveling a distance away from the 0 point will result in object sync'ed objects jumping or snapping to places. The x, y, and z values are treated independently, meaning that if you are at (0, 0, 200), then only the z position of the object will \"snap\" in place.\n\nExample world:\nwrld_312c666d-50c9-4456-9585-02da88e1a92e\n\nIn this world there are three locations each with a green pickup sphere. Join with at least 2 people to see the bug.\n\n(0, 0, 0): The pickup here will act normal on remote clients.\n\n(200, 0, 0): The pickup will \"snap\" about 1 decimeter on the x axis, but will be normal on the y and z axes.\n\n(200, 0, 200): The pickup will \"snap\" on both x and z axes.",
